# Testing

Tests live under the member they exercise; shared helpers must not be imported from
another member's `tests` directory. Use ordinary unit tests without external services.

```bash
uv run inv test.run --project packages/__NAME__-core
uv run inv test.all
uv run inv test.all --no-rtk
```

Every suite gets its own pytest process and member configuration. Add integration
prerequisites only when the product needs them. Test observable behavior and failure
paths rather than implementation wording. Before a release, build all member wheels,
install them in a clean environment, and import packages from outside this checkout.
